We're moving the beta branch build (0.1029) to the main branch with a couple added fixes. Below is the cumulative list of changes from the last main branch build (0.1021):

- Tasks screen - villagers are now sorted by relevant skill level; 
- Tasks screen - Show All button now allows to filter out villagers assigned to tasks; 
- New map navigation: 
- click LMB to select a group; 
- hold LMB to scroll the map; 
- click RMB to open minimenu; 
- hold RMB to give movement orders; 
- double click to enter Village Overview or Expedition Equip screen; 
- Updates to popup help to reflect the changes (more improvements to come); 
- Hotkeys to allow quick access to certain screens (consult in-game Help: Map & HUD - Controls); 
- Navigation Bar at the top to quickly access different panels; 
- Display improvements, input boxes and arrows on Move Stack panel (for moving items between windows); 
- Toggle button to filter out equipped items (on Inventory, Equipment and New Expedition panels); 
- Toggle buttons to allow or prohibit new food or fuel items that are added to a group's inventory (Manage Supplies panel). These settings should also persist after loading the game; 
- Tooltip - 2 step animation is now 1 step animation; 
- Added tooltips to difficulty options; 
- Added tooltips to food bonuses; 
- Research points from crafting lowered; 
- Victory points from items are now based on the amount & rarity of resources used to craft/build them; 
- Deity info screen (click on your god portrait on the HUD) which contains info about: 
- advancement victory (new victory type!); 
- story progress; 
- selected difficulty settings; 
- 1h axes - reduced damage; 
- 2h swords - increased damage; 
- Reworked some and added new creatures, groups and lairs; 
- Fixed a bug which caused a lot if Events not appear in game (you should notice new Events popping up!); 
- Building attraction dependent on starting village count; 
- Enemy spawning rate (not from lairs) decreased; 
- Number of possible lair spawns increased from 3 to 5; 
- Re-design of the Theodore Tutorial Event; 
- Re-design of the Hangedman quest; 
- Added several new events, with emphasis on early game; 
- rebalanced some resources that were considered not very useful (ie. Dryad Wood is now very light, Granite got a boost to amount gathered etc.); 
- Fixed resource icons staying on screen after opening UI panels;
- Fixed tutorial bug where boars kept spawning again and again after being killed;
- Fixed tutorial popup not appearing or appearing even if dismissed;
- Spears, staves etc. now additionally ignore shielding Defense (this type of damage is now called Piercing Damage);
- When an expedition ends its movement on a point of interest, the minimenu opens automatically;
- Reworded a couple skills mostly to improve understanding of Defense and Armour.

Hope you enjoy these. If you spot any problems - please report on the forums!
Thanks and have fun!

